{"@context":{"lean":"lean:","block":"block:","imports":{"@type":"@id"}},"@graph":[{"@id":"lean:module:QuantumObservableUniverses.Su2Emergence","@type":"LeanModule","name":"QuantumObservableUniverses.Su2Emergence","imports":["lean:module:Init","lean:module:QOU.Basic","lean:module:QOU.Glossary","lean:module:QOU.QuantumObservableUniverse.Structures","lean:module:Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Monoidal.Category","lean:module:Mathlib.CategoryTheory.Functor.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.CategoryTheory.NatTrans","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Group.Basic","lean:module:Mathlib.Algebra.Polynomial.Laurent"],"declarations":17,"chunks":1},{"@id":"lean:QOU.su2_emergence","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.su2_emergence","kind":"theorem","line":139,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/su2-emergence.lean#L139-L185","doc":"**The former `su2_emergence` axiom asserted nothing, and is now a\none-line theorem.**\n\nIt stood as\n\n    axiom su2_emergence … :\n      ∃ (sd : SpinDecomposition data.qou.C),\n        sd.fundamentalObj = data.qou.fundamentalObj\n\nwhich is **vacuously true**: `SpinDecomposition` has five fields, of\nwhich `simpleObj`, `fundamentalObj` and `adjointObj` are free and the\ntwo remaining are equations satisfiable by taking `simpleObj`\nconstant.  The witness below does exactly that, and the whole\nstatement closes by `rfl`.\n\nThis is not a false axiom -- it is worse in one respect and better in\nanother.  Better: nothing unsound was ever derivable from it.  Worse:\na false axiom announces itself the moment anyone looks for a\ncounterexample, while this one could stand indefinitely, cited as\nTannaka-Krein reconstruction, asserting only that a record with three\nfree fields can be filled in.\n\n**What the structure does not say.**  The old docstring described the\nconsequence as *\"simple objects indexed by half-integer spin labels\nwith dim = 2j + 1\"*.  `SpinDecomposition` carries **no** simplicity\ncondition, **no** injectivity of `simpleObj`, and **no** dimension\nfield -- so none of that is in the statement.  Encoding it is a\nstructure refactor and is deliberately not guessed at here; the\nTannaka duality and the SL(2) subgroup classification the proof\nsketch needs are genuinely absent from Mathlib, and that gap is\nreal.  What was not real is the suggestion that an axiom was\ncarrying it.\n\nLaTeX: `\\label{thm:su2-emergence}` ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SpinDecomposition.adjoint_is_one","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SpinDecomposition.adjoint_is_one","kind":"theorem","line":135,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/su2-emergence.lean#L135-L135","doc":"`Ad(A) = V_1` (the spin-1 representation). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SpinDecomposition.adjointObj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SpinDecomposition.adjointObj","kind":"def","line":133,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/su2-emergence.lean#L133-L133","doc":"The adjoint object `Ad(A)` corresponds to spin `1`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SpinDecomposition.fundamental_is_half","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SpinDecomposition.fundamental_is_half","kind":"theorem","line":131,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/su2-emergence.lean#L131-L131","doc":"`V = V_{1/2}` (the spin-1/2 representation). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SpinDecomposition.fundamentalObj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SpinDecomposition.fundamentalObj","kind":"def","line":129,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/su2-emergence.lean#L129-L129","doc":"The fundamental object `V` corresponds to spin `1/2`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SpinDecomposition.simpleObj","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SpinDecomposition.simpleObj","kind":"def","line":127,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/su2-emergence.lean#L127-L127","doc":"The simple object in `C` at spin label `j`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SpinDecomposition.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SpinDecomposition.mk","kind":"ctor","line":124,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/su2-emergence.lean#L124-L124","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.SpinDecomposition","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.SpinDecomposition","kind":"structure","line":118,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/su2-emergence.lean#L118-L135","doc":"**Spin decomposition** in a QOU: the simple objects of `C` are\nindexed by `SpinLabels`, and the fundamental object has spin `1/2`.\n\nMirrors the sibling `spin-labels.lean` definition; restated here so\n`su2_emergence` is self-contained (content-sibling `.lean` files\ncompile standalone and cannot import one another). ","formalizes":[{"@id":"block:prop:spin-labels","label":"prop:spin-labels","md":"quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/spin-labels.md"}],"signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.RankOneGaugeData.adjoint_trivial","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.RankOneGaugeData.adjoint_trivial","kind":"theorem","line":112,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/su2-emergence.lean#L112-L112","doc":"Adjoint vanishing: Hom(𝟙, Ad(A)) is trivial. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.RankOneGaugeData.volume_nondeg","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.RankOneGaugeData.volume_nondeg","kind":"theorem","line":102,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/su2-emergence.lean#L102-L102","doc":"Volume constraint: Λ²V → 𝟙 is non-degenerate (epimorphism).\n\n**No longer a hypothesis** (bean `qou-n1dj`, 2026-08-22).  Condition\n(iii) of `QuantumObservableUniverse` is now the isomorphism\n`volumeIso : exteriorSquare ≅ (𝟙_ C)`, and an isomorphism is epi, so\nthis field carries a default value and every QOU satisfies it.\n\nRead this together with the scope warning above.  `volume_nondeg` was\nthe *one* field of the three that constrained the QOU; with it\ndischarged, `RankOneGaugeData` adds nothing to\n`QuantumObservableUniverse`.  The content did not disappear — it moved\nupstream into the framework axiom, which is where the corpus states it —\nbut a reader told \"one of three constrains\" should now be told \"none of\nthe three, because the axiom already does\". ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.RankOneGaugeData.fund_dim_two","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.RankOneGaugeData.fund_dim_two","kind":"theorem","line":87,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/su2-emergence.lean#L87-L87","doc":"The fundamental representation V has categorical dimension 2,\nencoded as: the spin label for V is j = 1/2 (twice_j = 1). ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.RankOneGaugeData.qou","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.RankOneGaugeData.qou","kind":"def","line":84,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/su2-emergence.lean#L84-L84","doc":"The underlying QOU. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.RankOneGaugeData.mk","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.RankOneGaugeData.mk","kind":"ctor","line":82,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/su2-emergence.lean#L82-L82","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.RankOneGaugeData","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.RankOneGaugeData","kind":"structure","line":55,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/su2-emergence.lean#L55-L116","doc":"**Rank-1 characterisation** (hypotheses): in a QOU, the fundamental\nobject has categorical dimension 2, the volume form forces determinant 1,\nand adjoint vanishing forces the gauge group to be rank 1.\n\n**Scope warning — only one of the three fields constrains the QOU.**\nThe narrative above describes three constraints \"that together force\nSU(2)\"; the type delivers one:\n\n* `fund_dim_two` is an arithmetic fact about the *literal*\n  `{ twice_j := 1 }` and is discharged by `decide`.  It never mentions\n  `qou`, so it does **not** say that this QOU's fundamental object has\n  dimension 2 — the intended tie to `qou.fundamentalObj` is missing.\n* `volume_nondeg` is a genuine constraint on `qou.volumeForm`.\n* `adjoint_trivial` carries the default value `qou.adjoint_vanishing`,\n  so every QOU satisfies it automatically; it restates a QOU axiom\n  rather than adding a hypothesis.\n\nThe encoding gap in `fund_dim_two` is structural, not a typo: tying it\nto `qou.fundamentalObj` needs the spin indexing that `SpinDecomposition`\nsupplies, and that is the *conclusion* `su2_emergence` produces — so the\nhypothesis cannot reference it without circularity.  Restructuring is\ntracked as a bean; it is deliberately not done inline, because this is\nthe most depended-upon declaration on the critical path.\n\nConsequently `su2_emergence` should be read as \"volume non-degeneracy\n(plus the QOU axioms) yields a spin decomposition\", not as a\nthree-legged derivation. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.q_inv_param","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.q_inv_param","kind":"def","line":52,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/su2-emergence.lean#L52-L53","doc":"The inverse indeterminate `q⁻¹` of `R_q`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.q_param","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.q_param","kind":"def","line":49,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/su2-emergence.lean#L49-L50","doc":"The canonical indeterminate `q` of `R_q`. ","signatureChunk":0},{"@id":"lean:QOU.R_q","@type":"LeanDeclaration","name":"QOU.R_q","kind":"def","line":45,"sourceLink":"https://github.com/litlfred/qou/blob/7341d18daa5d103cc9fa41bebdf054eda96ad3d7/folio/quantum-observable-universe/quantum-observable-universes/su2-emergence.lean#L45-L47","doc":"Ground ring `R_q = ℤ[q, q⁻¹]` (Laurent polynomials over ℤ).\nSee `QOU.Archimedean.GroundRing` for the compiled definition. ","signatureChunk":0}]}